# PowerShell 7.6 LTS — Script Writing Skill

> **Effective Date:** June 2, 2026
> **Covers:** PowerShell 7.6.x (current LTS) — the ONLY version targeted by this skill.
> **Do NOT** write code compatible with Windows PowerShell 5.1 or earlier PowerShell 7.x releases unless the user explicitly asks for it.

---

## SYNOPSIS

This skill governs how to write, structure, and ship PowerShell scripts that target **PowerShell 7.6 LTS** exclusively. It covers:

- Version/environment requirements
- Installation methods (all platforms)
- Every new feature and breaking change in 7.6.x
- Script header mandatory boilerplate
- Best-practice patterns for modern PS7 code
- What to avoid (legacy 5.1 patterns, deprecated APIs)

---

## PART 1 — VERSION & RUNTIME REQUIREMENTS

### Current LTS Release (as of 2026-06-02)

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| **Current LTS** | PowerShell **7.6.2** |
| **Release date** | May 21, 2026 |
| **Runtime** | .NET 10.0.6 |
| **LTS supported until** | November 10, 2028 |
| **Previous LTS (still supported)** | 7.4.16 (expires Nov 10, 2026) |
| **Preview** | 7.7.0-preview.2 (NOT for production) |
| **GitHub releases** | https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases |

### Supported Operating Systems (7.6.x)

**Windows**
- Windows 10 (all editions, x64/x86/ARM64)
- Windows 11 (all editions)
- Windows Server 2019, 2022, 2025

**macOS**
- macOS 14 (Sonoma) and later — PKG now **notarized and signed by Microsoft**
- ARM64 (Apple Silicon) and x64

**Linux (officially supported)**
- Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04
- Debian 12, 13
- Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8, 9, 10
- openSUSE 15.6, 16.0
- Fedora 42, 43, 44

> **Important:** PowerShell 7.x installs into its **own directory** (`/opt/microsoft/powershell/7/` on Linux/macOS, `C:\Program Files\PowerShell\7\` on Windows) and runs **side-by-side** with Windows PowerShell 5.1. The executable is `pwsh`, never `powershell`.

---

## PART 2 — INSTALLATION (All Platforms)

### Windows — Fastest (winget)

```powershell
# Fresh install
winget install --id Microsoft.PowerShell --source winget

# Upgrade existing install
winget upgrade --id Microsoft.PowerShell

# If winget reports nothing available, refresh sources first
winget source update
```

> Windows 11 ships with winget. Windows 10 users need **App Installer** from the Microsoft Store first.

### Windows — Silent Enterprise MSI

```powershell
# MSI flags for enterprise deployment (x64 example)
$msiParams = @(
    '/package PowerShell-7.6.2-win-x64.msi'
    '/quiet'
    'ADD_EXPLORER_CONTEXT_MENU_OPENPOWERSHELL=1'
    'ADD_FILE_CONTEXT_MENU_RUNPOWERSHELL=1'
    'ENABLE_PSREMOTING=1'
    'REGISTER_MANIFEST=1'
    'USE_MU=1'
    'ENABLE_MU=1'   # Enables auto-updates through Windows Update
    'ADD_PATH=1'
)
msiexec.exe @msiParams
```

MSI packages available for **x64, x86, and ARM64** architectures.

### macOS

```bash
# Homebrew (recommended)
brew install --cask powershell

# Verify
pwsh --version

# Manual PKG (notarized, signed by Microsoft as of 7.6.2)
# Download from https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases
# ARM64:
curl -L -o /tmp/pwsh.pkg \
  https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases/download/v7.6.2/powershell-7.6.2-osx-arm64.pkg
sudo installer -pkg /tmp/pwsh.pkg -target /
```

### Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)

```bash
# Ubuntu 22.04/24.04
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y wget apt-transport-https software-properties-common
wget -q "https://packages.microsoft.com/config/ubuntu/$(lsb_release -rs)/packages-microsoft-prod.deb"
sudo dpkg -i packages-microsoft-prod.deb
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y powershell

pwsh --version
```

### Linux (RHEL/Fedora)

```bash
# RHEL 8/9/10
sudo rpm --import https://packages.microsoft.com/keys/microsoft.asc
curl -sSL -o /etc/yum.repos.d/microsoft.repo \
  https://packages.microsoft.com/config/rhel/9/prod.repo
sudo dnf install -y powershell

pwsh --version
```

### Verify Version After Install

```powershell
# Must show 7.6.x
$PSVersionTable
pwsh --version
```

---

## PART 3 — MANDATORY SCRIPT HEADER (7.6 Boilerplate)

Every script targeting PS 7.6 LTS **must** begin with this header:

```powershell
#Requires -Version 7.6
#Requires -PSEdition Core
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Brief one-line description of what this script does.
.DESCRIPTION
    Full description. Include purpose, dependencies, and any notes.
.PARAMETER ParameterName
    Description of each parameter.
.EXAMPLE
    .\MyScript.ps1 -Param1 Value
    Explanation of the example.
.NOTES
    Author:     <Your Name>
    Created:    <YYYY-MM-DD>
    Version:    1.0.0
    PS Version: 7.6.2 (LTS / .NET 10)
    Platforms:  Windows, Linux, macOS
#>
[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    # Parameters go here
)
```

> `#Requires -Version 7.6` will throw a clean error on older PowerShell instead of failing silently mid-script.
> `#Requires -PSEdition Core` blocks accidental execution under Windows PowerShell 5.1.

---

## PART 4 — WHAT'S NEW IN POWERSHELL 7.6 (Complete Feature Reference)

### 4.1 Updated Core Modules

| Module | Version in 7.6.2 | Notes |
|--------|-----------------|-------|
| **PSReadLine** | v2.4.5 | Tab completion, history, IntelliSense |
| **Microsoft.PowerShell.PSResourceGet** | v1.2.0 | Replaces PowerShellGet |
| **Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob** | v2.2.0 | **Replaces** the old `ThreadJob` module |

> **Breaking:** `ThreadJob` module is now `Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob`. If you use module-qualified cmdlet names, update from `ThreadJob\Start-ThreadJob` → `Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob\Start-ThreadJob`. The `Start-ThreadJob` cmdlet itself is unchanged.

### 4.2 New / Changed Cmdlet Parameters

```powershell
# Get-Clipboard — new -Delimiter parameter
# Split clipboard content on a custom delimiter
$items = Get-Clipboard -Delimiter ','

# Register-ArgumentCompleter — new -NativeFallback switch
# Register a catch-all completer for ALL native (non-PS) commands
Register-ArgumentCompleter -NativeFallback -ScriptBlock {
    param($wordToComplete, $commandAst, $cursorPosition)
    # your completion logic
}

# Join-Path — -ChildPath is now string[] (BREAKING CHANGE from 7.5)
# Old (still works): Join-Path C:\foo -ChildPath bar -AdditionalChildPath baz
# New (preferred):
Join-Path C:\foo bar baz    # Pass multiple child segments directly
$path = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'Documents' 'Projects' 'MyScript.ps1'

# New-Item — -Target is now treated as literal (no wildcard expansion)
New-Item -ItemType SymbolicLink -Path .\link -Target '.\some[dir]'  # safe now

# Get-Command — new -ExcludeModule parameter
Get-Command Get-Process -ExcludeModule Microsoft.PowerShell.Management

# Start-Process — -Wait polling is now more efficient (no busy-loop)
Start-Process notepad.exe -Wait

# Import-LocalizedData — now has implicit localization fallback
# Falls back to parent culture automatically (e.g. fr → en)
```

### 4.3 Engine Improvements

```powershell
# PSForEach() and PSWhere() — new aliases for intrinsic methods
# These are identical to .Where() and .ForEach() — just shorter aliases
$evens = (1..10).PSWhere({ $_ % 2 -eq 0 })
$doubled = (1..5).PSForEach({ $_ * 2 })

# [bigint] now supports thousands-separator syntax
$bigNum = [bigint]'1,000,000,000'   # valid in 7.6
$disk   = [bigint]'2,199,023,255,552'

# ConvertFrom-Json now ignores comments inside array literals
# Valid JSON5-style:
$json = '[/* a comment */ 1, 2, 3]'
$data = $json | ConvertFrom-Json   # no longer throws

# -Debug no longer triggers ShouldProcess prompt (long-standing bug fixed)
function Test-Debug {
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess)]
    param()
    Write-Debug "Debug message"
}
Test-Debug -Debug   # now shows debug msg, does NOT prompt

# Write-Host now respects $PSStyle.OutputRendering = 'PlainText'
$PSStyle.OutputRendering = [System.Management.Automation.OutputRendering]::PlainText
Write-Host "No ANSI codes in output"

# stderr output respects NO_COLOR environment variable
$env:NO_COLOR = '1'   # disables color in stderr

# PipelineStopToken — new property on Cmdlet for responsive pipeline stopping
# Use in C# cmdlet authors: this.PipelineStopToken.IsCancellationRequested

# Redirect to variable (now mainstream, was experimental)
# PSRedirectToVariable is now always-on:
$output = & { Write-Output 'hello'; Write-Error 'oops' } 2>&1
# Or redirect directly to variable:
Get-ChildItem *>&1 > $myVar   # supported redirect syntax

# Tilde expansion for native Windows executables (was PSNativeWindowsTildeExpansion)
# Now mainstream — ~ expands correctly when passed to cmd.exe, git, etc.
cmd /c echo ~\Documents   # expands properly

# PSFeedbackProvider — now mainstream
# Suggestions appear automatically when a command isn't found
```

### 4.4 Tab Completion Improvements (Dozens)

Key completions added/fixed in 7.6:

```powershell
# Aliases now expand to their resolved command in completions
# Module shortname completion (e.g. type "PSRes" → completes PSResourceGet)
# Variables inside ArrayLiteralAst and ParenExpressionAst complete correctly
# Scoped variables complete without needing to type the scope prefix
# Hashtable key completions now show tooltips
# Parameter HelpMessage used as completion tooltip
# -PropertyType argument completer for New-ItemProperty
# Quote-aware completions for -Noun (Get-Command), -PSEdition (Get-Module)
# Path completions fixed for wildcard paths in non-filesystem providers
# Duplicate command names no longer appear in completion results

# Example of what now works that didn't before:
$hash = @{ Name = 'Alice'; Age = 30 }
$hash.<TAB>   # now shows tooltips for each key
```

### 4.5 Experimental Features Promoted to Mainstream

These features are now **always on** in 7.6 — no `Enable-ExperimentalFeature` needed:

| Feature | What it does |
|---------|-------------|
| `PSFeedbackProvider` | "Did you mean...?" suggestions when commands not found |
| `PSNativeWindowsTildeExpansion` | `~` expands correctly in native Windows commands |
| `PSRedirectToVariable` | Redirect streams to variables with `>$var` |
| `PSSubsystemPluginModel` | Plugin model for subsystem extensibility |

### 4.6 Security & Infrastructure Improvements

```powershell
# AppContainer support — PS 7.6 now works inside Windows AppContainer sandboxes
# PSRP protocol updated — session key exchange deprecated between newer client/server
# Telemetry now respects Windows diagnostics/feedback setting
# Update notifications delayed 1 week to ensure package availability
# POWERSHELL_DIAGNOSTICS_OPTOUT env var — opt out of named-pipe listener
$env:POWERSHELL_DIAGNOSTICS_OPTOUT = '1'

# Out-GridView fixed — replaced legacy BinaryFormatter with secure custom impl
# Now fully functional on .NET 10 (was broken in earlier 7.x)
Get-Process | Out-GridView -Title "Processes"   # works again

# macOS PKG is now notarized and signed by Microsoft (no more Gatekeeper warnings)
```

---

## PART 5 — BREAKING CHANGES IN 7.6 (Must Know)

### BC-1: Join-Path -ChildPath is now `string[]`

```powershell
# OLD (7.5 and earlier) — required -AdditionalChildPath for multiple segments
$p = Join-Path C:\root -ChildPath foo -AdditionalChildPath bar, baz

# NEW (7.6) — pass all segments directly (array accepted)
$p = Join-Path C:\root foo bar baz
$p = Join-Path C:\root -ChildPath 'foo', 'bar', 'baz'
```

### BC-2: WildcardPattern.Escape() escapes lone backticks correctly

```powershell
# If your code relied on WildcardPattern.Escape() NOT escaping lone backticks,
# you must audit and fix those paths. Example:
[WildcardPattern]::Escape('path`name')
# 7.5: returned 'path`name'   (backtick not escaped)
# 7.6: returns  'path``name'  (correctly escaped)
```

### BC-3: ThreadJob module renamed

```powershell
# OLD module-qualified syntax:
ThreadJob\Start-ThreadJob -ScriptBlock { ... }

# NEW:
Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob\Start-ThreadJob -ScriptBlock { ... }

# Unqualified syntax unchanged — still works:
Start-ThreadJob -ScriptBlock { ... }
```

### BC-4: Trailing space removed from trace event source name

```powershell
# The GetHelpCommand trace source name no longer has a trailing space.
# Fix any string comparisons that depend on "GetHelpCommand " (with space).
```

---

## PART 6 — MODERN PS 7.6 PATTERNS & BEST PRACTICES

### Use `pwsh` not `powershell`

```powershell
# In scripts, shebang lines, CI configs:
#!/usr/bin/env pwsh

# In batch files / CMD:
pwsh -NonInteractive -File .\MyScript.ps1

# NEVER call 'powershell' for PS7 — that invokes Windows PowerShell 5.1
```

### Ternary Operator (7.0+, use freely)

```powershell
$result = $condition ? 'yes' : 'no'
$max = ($a -gt $b) ? $a : $b
```

### Null Coalescing (7.0+)

```powershell
$value = $possiblyNull ?? 'default'
$value ??= 'assign-if-null'
```

### Pipeline Chain Operators (7.0+)

```powershell
# && runs right side only if left succeeds
# || runs right side only if left fails
git pull && git status
Get-Process nonexistent || Write-Host "Not found"
```

### Foreach-Object -Parallel (7.0+, production-ready in 7.6)

```powershell
1..10 | ForEach-Object -Parallel {
    Start-Sleep -Milliseconds (Get-Random -Max 500)
    "Processed: $_"
} -ThrottleLimit 5
```

### PSForEach / PSWhere (7.6 NEW aliases)

```powershell
# Use instead of .Where() and .ForEach() for readability
$admins  = $users.PSWhere({ $_.Role -eq 'Admin' })
$names   = $users.PSForEach({ $_.Name.ToUpper() })

# Mode argument (First, Last, Until, SkipUntil, Split)
$first3  = $items.PSWhere({ $_.Active }, 'First', 3)
```

### Error Handling (7.x style)

```powershell
# Use -ErrorAction Stop + try/catch for all cmdlet errors
try {
    Get-Item 'C:\nonexistent' -ErrorAction Stop
}
catch [System.IO.FileNotFoundException] {
    Write-Warning "File not found: $_"
}
catch {
    Write-Error "Unexpected error: $_"
    throw
}

# -Debug no longer breaks ShouldProcess in 7.6 — safe to use
function Invoke-Deploy {
    [CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess, ConfirmImpact = 'High')]
    param([string]$Target)
    if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($Target, 'Deploy')) {
        # deploy logic
    }
}
```

### ConvertFrom-Json with Comments (7.6)

```powershell
# JSON with comments in arrays is now valid
$config = @'
[
    /* primary server */
    "server1.corp",
    // fallback
    "server2.corp"
]
'@ | ConvertFrom-Json
```

### Thread Jobs (7.6 — use module-qualified name)

```powershell
# Import correct module
Import-Module Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob

$job = Start-ThreadJob -ScriptBlock {
    param($n)
    1..$n | ForEach-Object { $_ * $_ }
} -ArgumentList 100

$result = $job | Wait-Job | Receive-Job
```

### PSResourceGet (replaces PowerShellGet)

```powershell
# 7.6 ships with Microsoft.PowerShell.PSResourceGet v1.2.0
# Use these instead of Install-Module / Find-Module
Find-PSResource    -Name 'Az' -Repository PSGallery
Install-PSResource -Name 'Az' -Scope CurrentUser
Update-PSResource  -Name 'Az'
Get-PSResource     -Name 'Az'
```

### Redirect to Variable (7.6 mainstream)

```powershell
# Capture all streams including errors
$allOutput = & {
    Write-Output "stdout line"
    Write-Error  "error line"
    Write-Warning "warning"
} *>&1

# Redirect error stream to variable
Invoke-RestMethod https://api.example.com *>&1 > $capturedOutput
```

### NO_COLOR Support (7.6)

```powershell
# Scripts that need to detect plain-text mode:
if ($env:NO_COLOR) {
    $PSStyle.OutputRendering = [System.Management.Automation.OutputRendering]::PlainText
}
```

---

## PART 7 — WHAT TO AVOID (Legacy 5.1 / Deprecated Patterns)

| Avoid | Use Instead |
|-------|------------|
| `powershell.exe` binary | `pwsh` |
| `Install-Module` | `Install-PSResource` |
| `Find-Module` | `Find-PSResource` |
| `ThreadJob\Start-ThreadJob` | `Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob\Start-ThreadJob` |
| `-AdditionalChildPath` in `Join-Path` | Pass multiple strings to `-ChildPath` |
| `Write-Host` for data output | `Write-Output` or `return` |
| `$Error[0]` for error inspection | `$_` inside `catch {}` block |
| `[void]` everywhere for suppression | Pipeline to `$null`: `... | Out-Null` or assign to `$null =` |
| `Get-WmiObject` | `Get-CimInstance` (WMI is removed in PS7) |
| `[System.Net.WebClient]` | `Invoke-WebRequest` / `Invoke-RestMethod` |
| `.Where({...})` / `.ForEach({...})` | `.PSWhere({...})` / `.PSForEach({...})` (7.6 aliases) |
| Backtick line continuation `` ` `` | Splatting `@params` or natural line breaks |
| `Enable-ExperimentalFeature PSFeedbackProvider` | Always-on in 7.6 |
| `#Requires -Version 5.1` | `#Requires -Version 7.6` + `#Requires -PSEdition Core` |

