## PART 9 — VERSION CHECK SNIPPET

Embed this in scripts that must self-verify at runtime:

```powershell
function Assert-PowerShell76 {
    $required = [version]'7.6.0'
    $current  = $PSVersionTable.PSVersion
    if ($current -lt $required) {
        throw "This script requires PowerShell $required or later. Current: $current. Install from: https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases"
    }
    if ($PSVersionTable.PSEdition -ne 'Core') {
        throw "This script requires PowerShell Core (pwsh), not Windows PowerShell."
    }
}
Assert-PowerShell76
```

