## PART 10 — QUICK REFERENCE CARD

```
INSTALL (Windows):   winget install --id Microsoft.PowerShell --source winget
UPGRADE (Windows):   winget upgrade  --id Microsoft.PowerShell
VERIFY:              pwsh --version   # expect 7.6.2
BINARY:              pwsh (NOT powershell)
RUNTIME:             .NET 10.0.6 (bundled)
LTS SUPPORT:         Until November 10, 2028
HEADER:              #Requires -Version 7.6 + #Requires -PSEdition Core

NEW IN 7.6:
  Get-Clipboard -Delimiter ','
  Register-ArgumentCompleter -NativeFallback
  Join-Path path seg1 seg2 seg3             # -ChildPath is now string[]
  New-Item -Target treated as literal
  Get-Command -ExcludeModule SomeModule
  .PSForEach({}) / .PSWhere({})             # new intrinsic aliases
  [bigint]'1,000,000'                       # thousands separator support
  ConvertFrom-Json handles array comments
  -Debug no longer triggers ShouldProcess
  Out-GridView fixed (BinaryFormatter removed)
  $env:NO_COLOR respected in stderr
  $env:POWERSHELL_DIAGNOSTICS_OPTOUT='1'   # opt out named-pipe listener
  macOS PKG notarized + signed by Microsoft

MODULES:
  PSReadLine          2.4.5
  PSResourceGet       1.2.0   (use Install-PSResource, not Install-Module)
  ThreadJob →         Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob 2.2.0

PROMOTED FROM EXPERIMENTAL (always-on):
  PSFeedbackProvider, PSNativeWindowsTildeExpansion,
  PSRedirectToVariable, PSSubsystemPluginModel

BREAKING CHANGES:
  Join-Path -ChildPath = string[] (drop -AdditionalChildPath)
  WildcardPattern.Escape() escapes lone backticks (audit wildcard code)
  ThreadJob → Microsoft.PowerShell.ThreadJob (module-qualified names)
  Trace source "GetHelpCommand" no longer has trailing space
```

